#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# add_sides

#% text
# `add_sides(rel, c)` adds c to every side of the equation or inequality rel.

#% text
# `add_sides(a == b, rel)` adds a and b to the two sides of rel (or, with an equation as second argument, its sides to those of rel).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
add_sides(x - 3 == 7, 3)
#% output
#= x == 10

#% cell
add_sides(a == b, c == d)
#% output
#= a + c == b + d

#% cell
add_sides(z == 7, y > m*x + b)
#% output
#= y + z > 7 + b + m*x

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `subtract_sides`, `multiply_sides`, `divide_sides`, `solve`
